{"type":"standard","title":"Peggy Flanagan","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Peggy Flanagan</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q21662866","titles":{"canonical":"Peggy_Flanagan","normalized":"Peggy Flanagan","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Peggy Flanagan</span></span>"},"pageid":48456774,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/2026PeggyFlanagan_%28newcropped%29.jpg/330px-2026PeggyFlanagan_%28newcropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":428},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/2026PeggyFlanagan_%28newcropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1978,"height":2566},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376961464","tid":"e0e8b12a-ba28-11f1-bcf2-e02baad47a8b","timestamp":"2026-09-27T04:06:56Z","description":"American politician and Ojibwe activist (born 1979)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peggy_Flanagan","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peggy_Flanagan?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peggy_Flanagan?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Peggy_Flanagan"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peggy_Flanagan","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Peggy_Flanagan","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peggy_Flanagan?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Peggy_Flanagan"}},"extract":"Margaret Flanagan is an American politician and Ojibwe activist serving since 2019 as the 50th lieutenant governor of Minnesota. A member of the Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party (DFL), Flanagan served in the Minnesota House of Representatives from 2015 to 2019. She is the Democratic nominee for US Senate in the 2026 Minnesota U.S. Senate race.","extract_html":"<p><b>Margaret Flanagan</b> is an American politician and Ojibwe activist serving since 2019 as the 50th lieutenant governor of Minnesota. A member of the Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party (DFL), Flanagan served in the Minnesota House of Representatives from 2015 to 2019. She is the Democratic nominee for US Senate in the 2026 Minnesota U.S. Senate race.</p>"}